y um you know i think roger  federer was a great communicator a  little bit of a messiah actually had  such a following i've always said he's  like a religion out there but um she  seems to have that little extra  something which is going to well i i  think she's going to be a great  communicator and the fans are going to  love her  so passionate about the women's game and  you must love the fact that we're all  talking about the women's game at the  moment more than the men's game when it  comes to the us open  well you know i think these things are  in cycles aren't they and there's been  certain periods and eras in time in the  tennis world where it felt like the  men's game was a little bit stronger  than the women's in terms of its appeal  and then it swung a little bit back the  other way and then suddenly we had roger  federer and novak djokovic and rafael  nadal coming onto the scene and suddenly  there was a big attention on that but of  course we had the williams sisters we've  had sharapova we've had hingis clysters  uh you know all sorts of great great  names in tennis but certainly i think  what emma has done in the last couple of  weeks is just bring women's tennis right  back up onto the front pages and in many  ways she knocked off the front pages uh  and the sports page is what novak  djokovic was trying to achieve because  he was trying to take a piece of history  in the men's game and that got a little  bit sidelined by what emma was doing so  you know i think as i said before i  think it's just what we need i think um  it's made it really exciting to look  forward to women's tennis in the future  and i think she will never ever be  playing on the back courts or the  outside courts ever again i think it's  center court all the way yeah it's  wonderful stuff isn't it and just  finally before we let you go um what  advice would you give to her because  she's really at the store incredibly at  the start of her glittering career now  and she is only  